    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d939">

                <pb facs="0999" n="987" xml:id="pg987"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.111 Habicht, Hermann: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-08">July 8,
                        1941</date>.<lb/>[Received July 8—6:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1322. As Soviet authorities have finally agreed to issue exit visas to Mrs.
                    Hermann Habicht and son and to Mrs. Robert Magidoff, please authorize immediate
                    issuance immigration visas and allot one non-preference Soviet Union quota
                    number for issuance to minor son of Mrs. Habicht.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
